+
+### Why CharacterSet is not applied to every item slot
+
+The inspected PC source calls `CreateEffectSetPlayer` with the BOOTS model type. Applying the same set callback to helm/armor/pants/gloves/weapons/wings would duplicate effects and violate ownership. FIX99 therefore guards the boot-only behavior instead of broadening it.
+
+## 4. New ground ItemEffects runtime
+
+New module: `graphics/PcGroundItemEffects.js`.
+
+### 4.1 LoadEffect ownership
+
+`ItemEffects.lua::LoadEffect` is consumed by settled world drops, matching `ZzzObject.cpp::MoveItems`.
+
+- item type is converted to PC model type with `MODEL_ITEM + itemType`;
+- no matching Lua row => no effect (fail closed);
+- effect group is separate from the BMD orientation node because the PC owner rotates the authored local spawn offset itself;
+- effects only begin once the create/drop rise reaches the settled state.
+
+### 4.2 CreateShiny branch
+
+Preserved source contract:
+
+- cadence: every **24 source FX ticks** = ~960 ms at 25 Hz;
+- two logical particles per emission (subtype 0 + subtype 1);
+- configured RGB, scale and height retained;
+- EffectType 1 -> FLARE, 2 -> FIRE, default/other -> LIGHT;
+- random authored local offset is rotated by the item angle before conversion to Web coordinates;
+- sprites/materials are pooled inside the owner.
+
+The custom FLARE source calls a stock path whose desktop constructor can depend on `Target` even though this custom call does not supply one. FIX99 does not reproduce a null-pointer failure; it preserves the supplied color/scale and proven fade behavior. This is explicitly a compatibility repair, not a claim that the entire stock particle family has been reproduced.
+
+### 4.3 CreateThunderBolt branch
+
+Preserved source density and cadence:
+
+- cadence: every **6 source FX ticks** = ~240 ms;
+- **500 energy points + 500 glow points per authored burst**;
+- energy lifetime: 120 source ticks;
+- glow lifetime: 20 source ticks;
+- glow scale = source scale × 1.4;
+- height and color × intensity retained.
+
+Instead of allocating 1,000 Three.js Sprite objects per burst, the same logical 1,000 points are stored in two retained GPU point layers. Ring slots match source lifetime/cadence (20 energy slots, 4 glow slots), so density is not reduced to gain FPS.
+
+## 5. Map FPS / allocation repair
+
+### `world/PcMapParticles.js`
+
+Affected existing owners include Icarus, Devil Square and Tarkan particle families.
+
+Before FIX99:
+
+- spawn frequently created `new SpriteMaterial` + `new Sprite`;
+- particle death removed the sprite and disposed the material;
+- Tarkan update branches used new arrays / `.map()` in hot particle loops.
+
+FIX99:
+
+- adds retained per-owner pools keyed by bitmap owner;
+- active global particle-budget accounting remains unchanged: budget is acquired only while active and released on recycle;
+- pooled inactive sprites do not consume active particle budget;
+- material/texture/blend/lifetime/spawn gates are retained;
+- velocity/light arrays are reused instead of allocated per FX tick;
+- final owner disposal still releases pooled GPU materials.
+
+### `world/PcLorenciaVisuals.js`
+
+- CreateFire/fire/smoke and waterspout bone smoke use retained pools;
+- dynamic light position/color ownership is preserved;
+- per-update velocity/light array churn is removed;
+- merchant retained light sprites stay independent;
+- no PoseBox/Object134 scenery fabrication is introduced.
+
+This is an allocation/GC/GPU-resource optimization. It does **not** remove authored particles or lower map quality.
